sections.body:
Units 49 and 50 built the state: `2^n` complex amplitudes, outcome `k` at
`ψ[k + 1]`, qubit `q` as bit `q` of `k`. This unit stays with **one qubit**,
a state `ψ = [α, β]` meaning `α|0⟩ + β|1⟩` with `|α|² + |β|² = 1`, and asks
how it changes. You need:

* matrix-vector products `U * ψ` and the conjugate transpose `U'`
  (`LinearAlgebra`, Core Julia unit 20);
* `tr(A)`, the trace (sum of the diagonal), also from `LinearAlgebra`;
* the Born rule of unit 49: outcome `k` has probability `|ψ_k|²`;
* comparing floating-point results with a tolerance: `isapprox(a, b;
  atol = t)` (or `a ≈ b`, which uses a relative tolerance of about
  `sqrt(eps())` and no absolute one).

