sections.body:
This unit puts the pieces of units 49 to 51 together: a gate `U` (a `2×2`
unitary, unit 51) acting on qubit `q` (bit `q` of every outcome, unit 50) of
an `n`-qubit state stored as `2^n` amplitudes (unit 49). It also uses:

* the bit operations of unit 50: `1 << q`, `k & m` (bits set in both),
  `k | m` (bits set in either);
* `kron` for the textbook operator `kron(op_{n-1}, ..., op_0)` (unit 50);
* `@allocated f(x)`, which reports the bytes a call allocates; measure it
  after a first call, which compiles (Core Julia unit 14, "Performance");
* `qr` from `LinearAlgebra`, which factors a matrix into an orthonormal `Q`
  and a triangular `R` (used here to make random unitary matrices).
